  title: 'Cost of Living in Singapore (Present Day) '
  info: 'Singapore is known for its high cost of living, driven by housing, transportation,
    and daily expenses. Rent varies by location, with private condos costing more
    than HDB flats. Public transport is affordable, but car ownership is expensive
    due to COE (Certificate of Entitlement) fees. Dining options range from budget-friendly
    hawker centers to high-end restaurants. Utilities, healthcare, and education
    also contribute to living expenses. Despite the high costs, Singapore offers
    strong infrastructure, safety, and quality of life, making it an attractive place
    for both locals and expatriates.  '
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cce8898b6e8aa4da6bb90f5e956f42e7, type: 3}
